Ways I know of to increase tameness:

Your pet eats.  Not an option with monsters that never
eat like an arch-lich.

Reading the BotD in the invocation if your pet is
undead.  (Hmmm, I don't know if L's count as undead,
but i suspect they do.  Nice to think that the
Invocation on the VS would increase the tameness of
such a pet).

Charm monster spell.  *Very* good idea to keep this
one fresh.  Create familiar spell doesn't apply to
monsters that are already pets, though.

Magic harp.  These have charges but they can be
recharged.



Ways I know of to reduce tameness:

"... chokes on the leash!" message.  No leash, not an issue.

Attacking a trapped pet can make it go wild.

Riding stuff that doesn't apply.  Saddles don't fit on Ls.

The big one is - Being on a different level than your
pet for enough turns gradually reduces tameness.  So
when you have a powerfull enough pet, make sure it
follows you from level to level.

And the non-obvious one - Dead pets are quite tame
compared to live pets.  Think of ways to instakill it
just in case.  Stoning grenades should work.



